      "message": " lookup is a pure, deterministic, side-effect-free function of its name (no env, clock, randomness, or external state), so the flag value is a constant `True`.\n- `CONFIG_NAME = \"unrelated\"`\n- `feature_flag(name: str = CONFIG_NAME) -> bool` \u2014 validates `name` (`TypeError` for non-`str`, `ValueError` for empty) and always returns `True`. No imports of `semkg_contract`; no runtime dependency on anything outside the file.\n\n**Checks** \u2014 I ran small local `python -c` checks only. The tool returned `{\"ok\": true, \"returncode\": 0}` for them, but did not surface stdout/stderr, and a follow-up `read_file` on the written path reported \"No such file or directory\" for that absolute path, while `os.path.exists` on the same path printed as part of an unobserved command. So I can confirm the `write_file` call reported success and the check command exited 0, but I could not independently re-read the file back through the available tools. No other files were created and no repository-wide tests were run."
    },
